============================================================
SECTION D: ATTENTION MASS ON THE ACTION AND ENVIRONMENT TOKENS
============================================================
Debate Sec 2.2, diagnostic 3: 'near-zero attention mass [on the action
token] is dispositive'. v2's predictor sequence is [env, action, 36 patches],
so the uniform baseline is 1/38 = 0.0263 and the env token is measured
alongside the action token. Their relative mass says whether the predictor
leans on WHAT was pressed or merely on WHICH GAME it is playing -- the
latter would be the dynamics-side analogue of the D3 recognition shortcut.

  layer 0: action token = 0.0339   env token = 0.1272  (uniform would be 0.0263)  <-- at/below uniform baseline
  layer 1: action token = 0.0234   env token = 0.0175  (uniform would be 0.0263)  <-- at/below uniform baseline
  layer 2: action token = 0.0198   env token = 0.0206  (uniform would be 0.0263)  <-- at/below uniform baseline

  average across layers: action 0.0257  env 0.0551  (ratio env/action = 2.14x)
  -> NOTE: the predictor attends to the environment token substantially more
     than to the action token. It may be modelling per-game average dynamics
     rather than the consequences of the specific action taken.

  -> WARNING: average attention mass on the action token (0.0257) is close to or below the uniform baseline (0.0263). Spatial tokens are not preferentially attending to the action.

